-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Page and the Curse of the Pharaoh
  Publisher   T.D.F. micro-visions, 2015
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Page and the Curse of the Pharaoh (2015-01-23)(T.D.F. micro-
              visions)(48K-128K).tap
  MD5         5237d25deb5ff67f461c7de61e5d2df3

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 set by Ynicky, faithfully, on a Layer 2 that holds
              the set's colour values: tiles overwrite, figures and items XOR
              value by value, as the set's planes do, so figures mix with
              painted scenery where they overlap, as they do on Spec256. Value
              FF shows the ULA below in the cell's own colours. The game's
              ULA+ palette is turned off, as Spec256 has none. Source:
              Enhanced colours: Ynicky (Spec256).

  Pace        original (-0.00% measured in JNext 1.1.104, against the original
              on a 48K machine, game state in lockstep)

  Changes     1.0: figures keep their white on a Layer 2 that repeats the
              game's XOR plots; the plots run at 28 MHz; the original loading
              screen; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt ROM (NextZXOS 26.11
              safe); the game's speed restored after every hook; two tested
              cheats; Enhanced, the Spec256 colours faithfully, off by default

  Note        Keys: menu 1 keyboard (Q up, A down, O left, P right, Space
              jump), 2 Kempston, 3 Sinclair. Default: the original look with
              the clash gone: each figure's pixels are repeated in white on
              Layer 2, scenery as the original, in the game's own ULA+ palette
              on a Next. Enhanced (off by default): the Spec256 colours as
              they are, ULA+ off. 30 levels; AY music and beeper. Fits a 1MB
              Next. Known issues: pace in JNext against the original, 15 runs
              of 800 updates over 5 levels, state in lockstep: whole runs
              -0.31 to -0.00%, quiet thirds -0.17 to +0.00%, busy thirds -0.84
              to -0.00%, slowest 20 updates +0.01%; where the original runs
              late the build is faster; default: ropes and pick-ups take a
              cell's colour, as in the original; Enhanced: figures mix colours
              over painted scenery, as Spec256 does. Missing: natural play
              past the first levels (others reached by a test poke); hardware
              untested, ULA+ included.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity

  The archive's POKEs for this release, each tested in the simulator, same
  keys with and without it, 4 levels x 3 seeds x 5,000 frames: Infinite lives
  (none lost against 34) and Immunity (11 lost against 34: as the archive
  says, fire, water and yellow spikes still kill). Both offered.

